Package: flatcor
Title: Objective Bayes for Linear Regression with Flat Correlations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Diemithry M.", "Kloppenburg", email = "diemithrykloppenburg@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayes factors and estimation for linear regression with
    objective priors that extend Jeffreys' flat correlation to several
    predictors. With more than one predictor not everything can stay flat,
    so three priors are built and validated side by side, all R-squared ~
    Beta(a, 1) with a uniform direction: flat partial r (a = k/2: every
    correlation matrix of the outcome and predictors equally likely, as
    rstanarm stan_lm with eta = 1, so each coefficient's partial correlation
    is flat for any number of predictors), flat R (a = 1/2) and flat
    R-squared (a = 1). There is no default prior. All give Bayes factors that
    need only R-squared, n and k, and a conditional test per coefficient;
    estimation samples the prior in its own coordinates (R and a direction)
    with Stan.
